/entity/E39PCGGfRt9pdkfk4jWRMCxpWC4https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/ontology/hasWork08iOnline version:aSpurlock, Hughes Hudson, 1919-tHousing credit, a rural-urban comparison.w(OCoLC)646135090 0aRural development research report ;vno. 6.  aC0bGPO  aHistoric Shelflist Drawer 68; HSL002; 20260706  aVEND01b2026052902783cam a2200505 i 00006661420260702103606.0790518s1979    dcub     b   f000 0 eng    a12256945089 agp^79012659  a(OCoLC)4978426z(OCoLC)1225694508  b20250  aGPObengerdacGPOdOCLCQdSYBdOCLCQdOCLCFdOCLCOdCODdSFRdOCLdCUTdAGLdOCLCOdOCLCQdOCLCOdOCLCLdAGLdGPO  apcc  an-us---  aGPOO 4aKF3826.R8bF50 aaHT392.A53bno.11  a0024-G-0214a105.40:110 aA 105.40:111 aFitzwilliams, Jeannette,eauthor.1https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PCjB3YDHhmcTPxbTvm76mHP10aUnmasking problems in rural health planning /cJeannette Fitzwilliams. 1a[Washington, D.C.] :bDepartment of Agriculture, Economics, Statistics, and Cooperatives Service,cMay 1979.  aiv, 23 pages :bmap ;c26 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aRural development research report ;vno. 11  a[1 cd]  aIssued May 1979.  aThis is a publication issued by the United States federal government or produced with federal funds.  aIn scope of the U.S. Government Publishing Office Cataloging and Indexing Program (C&I) and Federal Depository Library Program (FDLP).  aIncludes bibliographical references (page 18).  aBetter health care planning and delivery require the following adjustments: (1) use of disaggregated data, (2) flexibility in regulations, (3) adjustment of funding formulas, (4) establishment of subarea councils, (5) identification of major health service area rural types, and (6) improvement of data for small rural areas. 0aHealth planningzUnited StatesxRural conditions. 7aUnited States2fast1https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PBJtxgQXMWqmjMjjwXRHgrq0(OCoLC)fst012041551